SHA1: 824246c76f78c2b0e3ca798773cbc840bb278120
SHA256: 44068bc6bb8defc095dfa94aed8624f62e55b39b0160f740512dbe12d09a2822
Section: Tweaks
Homepage: https://github.com/ibrahim2100/Albrhi-Repo
Description: Download videos, no ads, skip the sponsored parts, background playback — in Arabic or English.
 .
 NO ADS
 Stopped at three points, because ads arrive by three routes and blocking one does
 nothing about the others: the app stops asking for ads at all, promoted rows are
 dropped from the feed by the identifier YouTube's own servers attach to them, and the
 player refuses ads before a video, mid-video, and the kind stitched into the stream.
 .
 SKIP THE SPONSORED PARTS
 Paid plugs, self-promotion and subscribe reminders are jumped over using segments
 other viewers submitted to SponsorBlock. A line names what was skipped and offers an
 undo, and each segment is coloured on the progress bar. Eight categories, each with
 its own switch. Your video is never sent: only four characters of its fingerprint,
 so the server cannot tell which video you are watching.
 .
 BACKGROUND PLAYBACK
 Audio keeps going when you leave the app or lock the screen.
 .
 QUIETER
 Silence the prompt to update, since updating removes this tweak. Optionally hide the
 paid-promotion banner — off by default, because it is a disclosure.
 .
 SETTINGS AND DIAGNOSTICS
 Hold two fingers anywhere in YouTube. Arabic and English with right-to-left layout,
 and a card that says whether everything attached to your build. The report is also
 written to Documents/AlbrhiYT-report.txt.
 .
 TESTED ON YouTube 21.30.5. Nothing is pinned to a version number: every class is
 looked up at runtime and skipped if it is not there.
 .
 DOWNLOADS
 Open the panel over a video and save it to Photos, at the quality you pick, up to
 1080p60. Above 360p YouTube sends picture and sound separately; both are fetched and
 joined on the device. No button is added to YouTube itself — the row is in our own
 panel, so it cannot stop working when YouTube renames a view.
 .
 Segment data from SponsorBlock (sponsor.ajay.app), CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. The coloured
 markers are derived from iSponsorBlock by Galactic Dev, GPLv3.
 .
 Developed by Ibrahim Ismail AL-Rahn. Free and open source under the GNU GPL v3.
